1. DEFINITIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

"Mod" means the Creative Admin software in any form, including its
compiled or packaged artifacts (.jar), source code, configuration
templates, assets, and documentation.

"You" means any individual or entity that accesses, downloads, installs, runs,
copies, or otherwise deals with the Mod, whether or not acting within
the permissions granted here.

"Author" means THEFricadelle, who holds the copyright in the Mod as a
whole and is the sole party entitled to grant, withhold, or withdraw the
permissions set out here.

"Contributor" means a person whose contribution has been merged into the Mod.
Contributors retain copyright in their own contribution, license it to the
Author under Section 5.2, and are credited in CONTRIBUTORS.md and benefit from
the modpack permission of Section 5.3. That credit acknowledges authorship of a
specific contribution; it confers no ownership, no co-maintainership, and no
right to grant any permission under this license.

"Maintaining Organization" means any organization, team, or platform account
under which the official repository or an Official Channel is hosted. Hosting
the Mod, administering its repository, or being described as a
maintainer or team member transfers no copyright, grants none of the
permissions reserved to the Author, and does not entitle that organization or
person to act as the Author. A member who contributes does so as a Contributor
under Section 5.2 like anyone else. Where such an organization is a legal
entity, it holds rights only under a separate written assignment signed by the
Author; this license neither creates nor evidences one.

"Official Channel" means a distribution channel operated or authorized by the
Author — currently CurseForge, Modrinth, and the official GitHub repository and
its Releases page.

"Official Build" means an exact, unmodified artifact of the Mod as
published by the Author on an Official Channel.

"Server Operator" means a person or entity that runs a Minecraft server whose
players are expected or invited to install the Mod, including hosting providers
acting on behalf of their customers.


2. GRANT OF USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------

2.1 GRANT

Subject to Section 3, the Author grants You a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
revocable, royalty-free right to (a) download the Official Build from an
Official Channel, and (b) install and run the Mod on Minecraft client(s) and
Minecraft server(s) that You own or operate, in any singleplayer world and on
any server You join, including monetized servers, provided the Mod itself is
not sold or paywalled.

2.2 DISTRIBUTION TO PLAYERS BY SERVER OPERATORS

The Mod is installed on the server by the Server Operator and is also useful on
the client, where launchers, hosting panels, or server-side sync mods may
deliver it to the players of a given server. Notwithstanding Section 3(a), a
Server Operator may transmit the Official Build to players connecting to that
Operator's own server — including through launcher, hosting-panel, or sync-mod
auto-synchronization — provided the build is unmodified, the transmission is
incidental to joining that specific server rather than a general-purpose
download, and all copyright, authorship, and license notices are preserved.

This covers that server's own players only. Publishing, cataloguing, mirroring,
or offering the Mod as a downloadable or "one-click install" product
independently of a customer's own server instance requires the Author's prior
written permission.

2.3 REVOCATION

The rights granted in Section 2.1 are revocable, but revocation is:

  (a) individual — effective only against a specific You, only upon written
      notice from the Author, with no blanket or silent withdrawal of the
      rights granted to the public at large;

  (b) prospective — it does not retroactively make unlawful any use that was
      compliant when it occurred; and

  (c) limited — it does not, by itself, affect (i) the modpack permission of
      Section 3(b) as it applies to any compliant modpack maintained by a third
      party, nor (ii) the ability of other users to keep running an Official
      Build they lawfully obtained.

Withdrawing the modpack permission from a given modpack maintainer requires
separate written notice to that maintainer, and does not apply retroactively to
modpack versions already published.

This Section is without prejudice to Section 6 (Termination), which operates
automatically upon breach.


3. RESTRICTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Except with the Author's prior written permission, You may NOT:

  (a) redistribute, re-upload, mirror, repackage, or otherwise make the Mod
      (compiled or source) available to third parties through any channel not
      authorized by the Author — including mod-hosting sites, modpack platforms,
      forums, file lockers, Discord servers, and torrents — SUBJECT TO the
      modpack permission of Section 3(b), the server-to-player distribution
      permitted by Section 2.2, and the contribution fork permitted by
      Section 5.1;

  (b) include the Mod in a modpack, EXCEPT on all of the following
      conditions, which are permitted without further request: the modpack
      references an Official Channel so the file is fetched from that channel
      at install time; the exact, unmodified Official Build is used; and all
      copyright, authorship, and license notices are preserved. Bundling the
      file into an exported or offline pack, re-hosting it on any other
      channel, or including a modified build is NOT covered by this permission
      and still requires prior written consent. This permission may be
      withdrawn from a given modpack maintainer as provided in Section 2.3;

  (c) sell, rent, sublicense, or otherwise commercialize the Mod
      itself, or bundle it with a paid product;

  (d) create, distribute, or publish derivative works, forks, or modified
      versions of the Mod or its source, EXCEPT for the contribution
      fork permitted by Section 5.1;

  (e) remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, authorship, or license notice,
      including the SPDX headers at the top of source files;

  (f) claim authorship of the Mod or any part of it, present it as
      Your own work, or reuse its source — in whole or in part, verbatim or
      substantially adapted — inside any other project, product, or service;

  (g) use the name "Creative Admin", its former name "Arcadia Creative
      Admin", the Mod's current or former mod id, logo, visual identity, or
      any confusingly similar designation to identify or promote another
      project, product, or service, to suggest affiliation with or
      endorsement by the Author where none exists, or as or within a trademark,
      domain name, or account name. Factual, nominative references — stating
      that a modpack includes it, writing a tutorial, or publishing a review —
      are permitted and are not restricted by this paragraph;

  (h) use the Mod or its source, in whole or in part, as training,
      fine-tuning, validation, or retrieval corpus for any machine-learning or
      generative artificial-intelligence system, nor include it in any dataset
      compiled or distributed for that purpose. Ordinary use of AI-assisted
      developer tooling by a contributor working on a contribution under
      Section 5.1 is not restricted by this paragraph.


