5. CONTRIBUTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------

5.1 CONTRIBUTION FORK (LIMITED PERMISSION)

Notwithstanding Section 3(d), the Author grants You permission to fork the
official source repository and modify Your fork FOR THE SOLE PURPOSE of
preparing and submitting a pull request to the official repository, subject to
all of the following:

  (a) the fork stays a recognizable fork of the official repository and keeps
      this LICENSE file, the copyright notices, and the Mod's
      identity (name, mod id, branding) unchanged;

  (b) You do not distribute, publish, advertise, or release any build —
      compiled or source — produced from Your fork to third parties; the fork
      is for development and review only;

  (c) You do not use the fork as the basis of a separate, competing, or
      rebranded project; and

  (d) once Your pull request is merged, closed, or abandoned, this permission
      covers no further use of the fork beyond keeping it as a historical
      record. A pull request is "abandoned" if it has received no commit,
      comment, or other activity from You for ninety (90) consecutive days, or
      if You publicly state that You no longer intend to pursue it.

Any use of a fork outside these conditions is not licensed and falls back under
the restrictions of Section 3.

5.2 GRANT OVER YOUR CONTRIBUTION

If You submit a contribution (a pull request, patch, or code suggestion), You
grant the Author a perpetual, worldwide, irrevocable, non-exclusive,
royalty-free, sublicensable and transferable license to use, reproduce, modify,
relicense, and distribute it as part of the Mod under this or any
other license, without obligation of compensation. You confirm that You are the
author of the contribution, that You have the right to grant that license, and
that it includes no third-party code You are not entitled to submit.

To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law You waive any moral rights
You hold in Your contribution as against the Author and its licensees. Where
such rights cannot lawfully be waived, You agree not to assert them in a manner
that would prevent the Author from exercising the license granted above, it
being understood that the Author will not misattribute Your contribution to a
third party.

You retain the copyright in Your own contribution. Submitting one grants You no
ownership, no co-authorship, no right to redistribute, publish, mirror,
relicense, or fork the Mod, and no other right over it. A
Contributor's permissions over the Mod are exactly those of any other
You under Sections 2 and 3, neither more nor less. Having a contribution merged
does not enlarge them.

5.3 RECOGNITION OF CONTRIBUTORS

  (a) CREDIT. Every Contributor whose contribution is merged into the
      Mod is credited in the CONTRIBUTORS.md file distributed with
      it, by the name or handle they chose and with a description of what they
      contributed, so the credit identifies the work and not only the person.
      The Author will not misattribute a contribution to a third party. A
      Contributor may ask, through the official issue tracker, to be listed
      under a different name or handle, to have a contact address removed, or
      not to be listed at all.

  (b) MODPACK PERMISSION. Once a Contributor's pull request has concluded —
      merged, closed, or abandoned within the meaning of Section 5.1(d) — that
      Contributor may include the Mod in a modpack they publish, on
      the conditions of Section 3(b): Official Channel reference, exact
      unmodified Official Build, notices preserved. Having forked under Section
      5.1 never removes this permission, and Section 5.1(b) continues to bar
      distributing any build produced from that fork. This Section grants no
      right beyond what it states; bundling into an exported or offline pack,
      re-hosting elsewhere, or publishing a modified build still requires prior
      written permission under Section 3.


6. TERMINATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------

Any breach of this license automatically and immediately terminates the rights
granted in Sections 2.1, 2.2, 3(b), 5.1, and 5.3(b). You must then stop using
and delete all copies of the Mod in Your possession, and cease any distribution
then in progress.

Sections 1, 3, 4, 5.2, 5.3(a), and 7 through 11, together with the reservation
of rights stated above, survive termination. A Contributor's credit under
Section 5.3(a) is an acknowledgment of authorship and is not withdrawn by
termination. Termination is without prejudice to any other remedy available to
the Author.


